    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0386" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/7–1549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-15T19:00:00+01:00">July 15, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2789. Rumbold<anchor n="1" xml:id="d192-f1"/> informed us Foreign Office
                    instructed British Ambassador Athens to urge upon Greek Government that it
                    endeavor to avoid further Yugoslav frontier incidents. He indicated that this
                    was result of Bevin’s concern this regard and British desire that “in long run
                    Greek and Yugoslav Government get on.” According Rumbold Pipinelis assured
                    British Ambassador Greeks would endeavor prevent further incidents.</p>
                <p>Rumbold said Foreign Office has now also instructed British Ambassador Belgrade
                    to urge Yugoslavs on appropriate occasion not to <pb facs="0387" n="371"
                        xml:id="pg371"/> exaggerate Greek-Yugoslav frontier incidents but to discuss
                    such matters with Greeks along lines of meeting re Skočiver incident.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d192-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 2789, repeated Athens 41, Belgrade 59.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d192-f1" n="1" xml:id="d192-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Horace Anthony Rumbold, Head of the Southern Department, British Foreign
                    Office.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d192-f2" n="2" xml:id="d192-f2-content">
                <p>Regarding the meeting on the Skočivir incident, see footnote 5 to telegram 1335,
                    July 12, from Athens, <ref target="#pg367">p. 367</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
